# =====================
# cloudflare tunnel token.
#
# SECRET — never commit a real token. copy this file to `.env` and
# paste your tunnel token there; `.env` is gitignored.
#
# where to get it: cloudflare dashboard > Zero Trust > Networks >
# Tunnels > your tunnel > the docker install command shows
#   --token <THIS VALUE>
#
# the variable is named TUNNEL_TOKEN (not CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN)
# because that is the name cloudflared itself reads from the
# environment, and docker-compose.yml hands this file to it verbatim
# via env_file. renaming it here would mean the container starts with
# an empty token.
# =====================
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# =====================
# the public url of the deployed site.
#
# OPTIONAL — used by DOCKER/deploy.sh to check that the live site
# serves the bundle the local build produced. leave it empty to skip
# that check (the script then reports the local build hash instead).
#
# it is NOT baked into the repo on purpose: the url belongs to whoever
# deploys, so set it in your own `.env` (gitignored) or pass it inline
# as `FASTDATA_SITE_URL=... bun run deploy`.
# =====================
FASTDATA_SITE_URL=
# =====================
